I have opened a PR fixing this: https://github.com/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/pull/33832

The fix adds `X = X - self.X_offset_` before the variance computation in both `BayesianRidge.predict` and `ARDRegression.predict`. During `fit()` the model centers `X` before computing `sigma_`, so `predict()` must apply the same centering before evaluating the predictive variance. Tests added confirm that std is minimized near training data, not near the origin.

